    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d531">

                <pb facs="0788" n="774" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg774"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.83/5–1447: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Durbrow</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-05-14">May 14, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1772. May 6 [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pravda</hi> May 14 carries following Tass denial: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Tass is authorized to state report of Cairo paper <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Al-Ahram</hi> to effect that in Stalin’s
                            conversation with Bevin Soviet Govt promised not to support Egypt in UN,
                            does not correspond to facts.</p>
                        <p>“Conversation did not touch upon question of UN, or of support or
                            non-support by USSR of any Egyptian demand in UN.</p>
                        <pb facs="0789" n="775" xml:id="pg775"/>
                        <p>“It was stated with regard to relations between Britain and Egypt that
                            this was affair of Britain and Egypt, and USSR, in accordance with its
                            unchanged policy of non-intervention, does not think of intervening in
                            this matter.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Durbrow</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
